<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhodesian Bush War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1964–1979</span> · Also known as Second Chimurenga, Zimbabwe War of Liberation</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Rhodesian Bush War was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> war fought by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-national-union">ZANU</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe-african-peoples-union">ZAPU</a> nationalist movements against the white minority government of Rhodesia. It intensified after 1972, with guerrillas operating from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mozambique">Mozambique</a>; tens of thousands died. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancaster-house">Lancaster House</a> Agreement of 1979, which led to majority rule and the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> in 1980.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhodesian-bush-war.jpg" alt="Rhodesian Bush War" width="320" height="305" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kelly The Angel · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RhodesiaAllies1975-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
